    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (87.04) and **James Wood** (78.42) headlining our offensive attack. **Corbin Carroll** is our strongest play, leveraging a prime spot in the three-hole against Ure\u00f1a, whose 4.65 xERA suggests plenty of run-scoring opportunities. His elite xwOBA of 0.370, combined with his unparalleled ability to steal bases\u2014a category we are aggressively prioritizing\u2014makes him the anchor of our lineup. Similarly, **James Wood** offers significant upside at the leadoff spot; facing a vulnerable starter in Spence (6.03 xERA) provides a massive efficiency boost, and his elite 0.403 xwOBA ensures he remains a high-floor start despite his youth. **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Gabriel Moreno** also provide excellent utility value today, both benefiting from favorable park factors and high-leverage spots in the batting order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the periphery involved **Dalton Rushing** (55.47), who narrowly outpaced the likes of **Alex Freeland** (52.50) and **Henry Bolte** (47.80) to secure a starting role. While **Dalton Rushing** suffers from an unfavorable batting order position at #8, his platoon advantage and the positive matchup against Martinez, N provide enough of a cushion to justify the start over players like **Kyle Karros** (47.84) or **Zach McKinstry** (42.41), both of whom are relegated to the bottom of the order and face tougher situational hurdles. We are currently navigating a depleted bench; with **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined by injuries, and **Josh Naylor** and **Jose Caballero** observing an off-day, our depth is tested. We remain monitor-heavy on the waiver wire for prospects like **Carson Williams**, **Cole Young**, or **Travis Bazzana** to bolster the roster alongside veterans like **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, and **Max Muncy** as we fight to preserve our daily game caps while maintaining our edge in the stolen base department.",
